<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vyborg</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Viipuri, Viborg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vyborg, in Finnish Viipuri, is a port city at the head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-finland">Gulf of Finland</a> on the Karelian Isthmus, now in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. It grew around a castle founded by the Swedes in 1293, passed to Russia in 1710 and became part of the Grand Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> in 1812. As one of Finland's largest cities it was ceded to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> in 1940, retaken in 1941 and finally lost in 1944, when its Finnish population was evacuated.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vyborg.jpg" alt="Vyborg" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: A.Savin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vyborg_June2012_View_from_Olaf_Tower_05.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
